        "answer": {
          "short": "$0,1,4,5,6,9$.",
          "worked": "The last digit of a square depends only on the last digit of the original number. Squaring each possible final digit gives:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}0^2&=0\\\\1^2&=1\\\\2^2&=4\\\\3^2&=9\\\\4^2&=16\\\\5^2&=25\\\\6^2&=36\\\\7^2&=49\\\\8^2&=64\\\\9^2&=81\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe possible last digits are $0,1,4,5,6,9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
